 ```
 
+#### `downscale`
+
+Controls the resolution of the final cached blur texture.
+The default value of `2` keeps the result at half resolution and lets the compositor linearly upscale it while drawing.
+Since blurred images contain little high-frequency detail, this usually looks very close to full resolution while avoiding the most expensive upsampling pass and reducing output texture memory by 75%.
+
+Use `1` for full-resolution output. Powers of two are supported; other values are rounded down to the nearest power of two.
+The value cannot skip more levels than configured by `passes`.
+
+```kdl
+blur {
+    downscale 2
+}
+```
+
 #### `noise`
 
 Amount of noise to add on top of the blur.
